---
import BlogArticle from "../../components/BlogArticle.astro";
---

<BlogArticle
	title="How to Correct or Update the Photo or Signature on a PAN Card"
	description="Learn how to request a PAN photo or signature correction, choose the correct change request instead of a reprint, and prepare supporting files."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/blogs/update-pan-photo-signature/"
	heading="How to correct or update the photo or signature on a PAN card"
	intro="A replacement card does not by itself change the photo or signature held in the PAN record. If the record needs an image update, use the provider’s change/correction route and follow its current document instructions."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Reprint or correction: choose the right service</h2>
		<p>
			Use a reprint request when the PAN details are already correct
			and you only need another physical card. Use a change/correction
			request when you need the PAN record or card to show a corrected
			detail, including a photo or signature if the current form offers
			that option. A reprint-only request is not a substitute for
			updating stored information.
		</p>
		<p>
			Use the correction service associated with your provider. UTIITSL
			currently labels its Indian correction route CR-01/CR-02; Protean
			lists a separate “Change/Correction in PAN Data” service. Do not
			apply for a new PAN just to update an existing PAN record.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">General steps to request an image update</h2>
		<ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
			<li>Open the official provider’s change/correction service and select the form for your applicant type.</li>
			<li>Enter the existing PAN and applicant details exactly as requested. Verify the PAN before paying or submitting.</li>
			<li>Choose the photo and/or signature update option if it appears on the current form. Select only the changes you actually need.</li>
			<li>Prepare the image in the format, dimensions, file-size limit, and background specified by that live form. Older online guides may quote outdated size limits.</li>
			<li>Attach any identity, address, or other supporting evidence requested by the correction route. Confirm whether the workflow uses electronic verification or requires signed/physical documents.</li>
			<li>Review the preview and declaration, submit the request, save the acknowledgement number, and track the application through the provider.</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Prepare a clear photo or signature file</h2>
		<p>
			Use a recent, well-lit photo with a plain background, and crop
			without stretching or cutting off the subject. For a signature,
			scan or photograph the actual signed paper, keep the full
			handwriting visible, and avoid editing the signature into a
			different shape. A <a class="text-link" href="/#photo-tool">PAN card photo resizer</a>
			or <a class="text-link" href="/#photo-tool">PAN card signature resizer</a>
			can help prepare an image file; it cannot file a correction
			request or guarantee that the provider will accept it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<p>
		Check the official <a class="text-link" href="https://tinpan.proteantech.in/services/pan/pan-index.html">Protean PAN service options</a>
		or the <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pan.utiitsl.com/PAN/csf.html">UTIITSL correction page</a>
		for the current route and instructions. Fees, identity checks, file
		rules, and processing steps can change.
	</p>
</BlogArticle>
